---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Resume — TJ Nicolaides"
  description="Resume for TJ Nicolaides, Engineering Manager at Airbnb. 15+ years of full-stack engineering across web, iOS, and Android. Based in Ardmore, PA."
>
  <main class="resume">
    <a href="/" class="back">← tjnicolaides.com</a>

    <header class="resume-head">
      <h1>TJ Nicolaides</h1>
      <p class="resume-contact">
        Ardmore, PA
        · <a href="mailto:tj.nicolaides@gmail.com">tj.nicolaides@gmail.com</a>
        · <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/tnicolaides/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>
        · <a href="https://github.com/tjnicolaides" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
      </p>
    </header>

    <section aria-labelledby="h-profile">
      <h2 id="h-profile">Profile</h2>
      <p class="profile-text">
        Engineering leader with 15+ years building products at scale and the teams that make them.
        Operates as a player-coach: close enough to the technical work for judgment to be credible,
        far enough out to grow engineers and shape direction. At Airbnb, designed and shipped
        Airbnb-Friendly Apartments, a new marketplace segment, then moved into engineering management
        to expand the program internationally and grow the team that owns it. Brings a hands-on
        leadership style, cross-functional range, and a conviction that the best technical outcomes
        come from happy, well-sized teams with real ownership, clear craft standards, and a bias
        toward boring technology.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="h-experience">
      <h2 id="h-experience">Experience</h2>

      <article>
        <div class="role-header">
          <div>
            <h3>Engineering Manager</h3>
            <span class="employer">Airbnb</span>
          </div>
          <time>July 2024 – Present</time>
        </div>
        <p class="role-summary">
          Lead a team of 7 engineers within the Real Estate organization, operating across the
          Airbnb-Friendly Apartments program — a marketplace connecting multifamily property managers
          with Airbnb's host network, now spanning 1,300+ buildings across 75+ international markets
          and generating ~$13M in annual host earnings.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Led program internationalization, expanding Airbnb-Friendly Apartments from a US-only product to markets in the UK, Brazil, and Canada. Required significant refactoring of legacy payout infrastructure originally built in 2018 with hard-coded US-market assumptions. Grew the program to 1,300+ buildings across 75+ international markets in the process.</li>
          <li>Delivered the Airbnb-Friendly Partner Tools dashboard, a ground-up rewrite of a performance-constrained internal product used by property managers to track hosting activity, bookings, and program value. Adopted new read-optimized data pipelines and rebuilt the UI against new APIs, replacing a tool the team had been working around for years.</li>
          <li>Stepped into full product management responsibilities during the embedded PM's extended leave. Authored requirements documentation, facilitated on-site roadmapping sessions, and maintained sprint continuity across engineering and stakeholder teams. Kept the product moving without losing the team's trust or momentum.</li>
          <li>Built the team's hiring pipeline end-to-end. Sourced, interviewed, and onboarded two new engineers and one internal transfer, advanced one engineer to Senior, and managed a performance separation with care. Made the hard calls and the welcoming ones with equal weight.</li>
          <li>Coach engineers across the seniority spectrum, with two on the senior track and two more targeting staff-level scope. Focus is on technical judgment, written communication, and the glue work that makes the team more than the sum of its parts.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article>
        <div class="role-header">
          <div>
            <h3>Senior Software Engineer — Technical Lead</h3>
            <span class="employer">Airbnb</span>
          </div>
          <time>August 2019 – June 2024</time>
        </div>
        <p class="role-summary">
          Technical lead for Airbnb's Real Estate engineering organization, with a primary focus on
          the Airbnb-Friendly Apartments marketplace — a product enabling multifamily property owners
          to authorize and encourage tenants to host on Airbnb.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Designed and led the full-stack implementation of Airbnb-Friendly Apartments from inception through launch. The product debuted with 175+ buildings across 25+ US markets. Coordinated across design, legal, go-to-market, accessibility, and executive stakeholders.</li>
          <li>Architected GraphQL APIs and web applications underpinning the marketplace, working across backend, iOS, and Android platforms to keep the host experience coherent across three client surfaces.</li>
          <li>Led migration of multifamily host enrollment tools ahead of the publicly launched List Your Space 2.0 and Manage Your Space 2.0 initiatives, delivering on a hard deadline with no room to slip.</li>
          <li>Stewarded the frontend engineering guild within the Real Estate organization. Mentored new hires and backend engineers expanding their client-side skills and helped them build real confidence on the client side.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article>
        <div class="role-header">
          <div>
            <h3>Software Engineer</h3>
            <span class="employer">Urbandoor <span class="acquired">(acquired by Airbnb, August 2019)</span></span>
          </div>
          <time>March 2019 – August 2019</time>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>Built a redesigned, high-performance Provider Tools experience enabling multifamily partners to customize guest data views within the Urbandoor platform, using Vue.js, Ruby on Rails, and PostgreSQL.</li>
          <li>Led a holistic regression and defect sprint addressing globalization issues across the application ahead of acquisition.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article>
        <div class="role-header">
          <div>
            <h3>Director, Software Development</h3>
            <span class="employer">Think Company</span>
          </div>
          <time>January 2017 – February 2019</time>
        </div>
        <p class="role-summary">
          Led a department of 14 software developers and one development manager at a Philadelphia-based
          design and technology consultancy, serving clients across healthcare, financial services,
          insurance, and enterprise sectors.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Owned recruiting, hiring, and onboarding for all software development roles. Guided technical project outcomes by advancing frontend development and consulting practices across the team.</li>
          <li>Co-created a software development apprenticeship program pairing junior developers with senior engineers for structured mentorship and on-the-job training.</li>
          <li>Provided ongoing performance feedback, career coaching, and professional development planning across the team.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article>
        <div class="role-header">
          <div>
            <h3>Technical Lead</h3>
            <span class="employer">Think Company</span>
          </div>
          <time>September 2014 – December 2016</time>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>Led project teams delivering pattern libraries, CMS templates, custom APIs, and JavaScript prototype applications for clients including AM Resorts, ADP, TE Connectivity, Health Advocate, and Janssen Pharmaceuticals.</li>
          <li>Templatized LAMP development and staging environment provisioning for studio projects, materially reducing onboarding time for new engineers joining client engagements.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article>
        <div class="role-header">
          <div>
            <h3>Developer</h3>
            <span class="employer">LabRetriever Sleep EMR</span>
          </div>
          <time>May 2012 – September 2014</time>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>Built features and user experiences for a cloud-based sleep lab management platform (CakePHP, MySQL, jQuery), including a redesigned appointment calendar and integrations with HL7 billing systems and shipping APIs.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article>
        <div class="role-header">
          <div>
            <h3>Interactive Technology Manager</h3>
            <span class="employer">Greater Media Philadelphia</span>
          </div>
          <time>August 2008 – May 2012</time>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>Developed and maintained web, podcast, and live-streaming products for WMMR, WMGK, BEN-FM, and 97.5 The Fanatic. Built Android live-streaming applications for each station and contributed code reused across Greater Media's national market clusters.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="h-skills">
      <h2 id="h-skills">Technical Skills</h2>
      <dl class="skills-grid">
        <div class="skill-row">
          <dt>Languages & Runtimes</dt>
          <dd>TypeScript, JavaScript, Node.js, Kotlin, Java, Python, Ruby</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="skill-row">
          <dt>Frontend & APIs</dt>
          <dd>React, Vue.js, GraphQL, Progressive Web Applications, REST</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="skill-row">
          <dt>Mobile</dt>
          <dd>Android (native)</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="skill-row">
          <dt>Infrastructure & Platforms</dt>
          <dd>Kubernetes, Docker, PostgreSQL, MySQL, nginx</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="skill-row">
          <dt>AI-Assisted Development</dt>
          <dd>Claude Code, GitHub Copilot, Cursor; agentic workflow design, prompt engineering for technical specs and code review</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="skill-row">
          <dt>Practices</dt>
          <dd>Technical design & architecture review, engineering hiring, career development, accessibility (WCAG), internationalization, boring-technology principle, monolith-first architecture</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="h-education">
      <h2 id="h-education">Education</h2>
      <div class="edu-header">
        <div>
          <p class="degree">B.A., Communication Studies</p>
          <p class="minor">Minor: Web Technology</p>
          <p class="school">West Chester University of Pennsylvania</p>
        </div>
        <time>June 2006</time>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="h-community">
      <h2 id="h-community">Community & Speaking</h2>
      <p class="community-text">
        Technical speaker and event co-organizer: Barcamp Philly, Girl Develop It, Launch Academy,
        Zip Code Wilmington, Tech In Color, PWA Philly. Judge of Elections, Montgomery County, PA.
        Adjunct Professor, University of the Arts Continuing Education (2012–2014).
      </p>
    </section>

    <footer class="resume-footer">
      <a href="/">← Back</a>
      <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/tnicolaides/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>
    </footer>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  :global(body) {
    align-items: flex-start;
  }

  :global(main.resume) {
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(32px, 7vw, 44px);
    line-height: 1;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  h2 {
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    padding-bottom: 10px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--surface);
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 10.5px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h3 {
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin-bottom: 3px;
  }

  .back {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 48px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: color 0.15s;
  }

  .back:hover {
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  .resume-head {
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }

  .resume-contact {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  .resume-contact a {
    color: var(--muted);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: color 0.15s;
  }

  .resume-contact a:hover {
    color: var(--accent-hi);
  }

  section {
    margin-bottom: 52px;
  }

  .profile-text {
    color: color-mix(in oklch, var(--fg) 70%, var(--bg));
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    padding-left: 18px;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  article {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  article:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .role-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 24px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .employer {
    display: block;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--accent-hi);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }

  .acquired {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  time {
    font-size: 10.5px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    white-space: nowrap;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    padding-top: 4px;
  }

  .role-summary {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    color: color-mix(in oklch, var(--fg) 65%, var(--bg));
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 16px;
    color: color-mix(in oklch, var(--fg) 60%, var(--bg));
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  li::before {
    content: '·';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .skills-grid {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
  }

  .skill-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr;
    gap: 16px;
    align-items: baseline;
  }

  dt {
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: color-mix(in oklch, var(--fg) 65%, var(--bg));
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .edu-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 24px;
  }

  .degree {
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin-bottom: 3px;
  }

  .minor {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }

  .school {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--accent-hi);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .community-text {
    color: color-mix(in oklch, var(--fg) 60%, var(--bg));
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .resume-footer {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    margin-top: 16px;
    padding-top: 32px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--surface);
  }

  .resume-footer a {
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    color: var(--muted);
    text-decoration: none;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    transition: color 0.15s;
  }

  .resume-footer a:hover {
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .role-header,
    .edu-header {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 4px;
    }

    .skill-row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 4px;
    }
  }
</style>
